<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-French War (1213–1214)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1213">1213</a>–<a href="/years/1214">1214</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-French War of 1213–1214 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, allied with Emperor Otto IV and the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Boulogne</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a>. John aimed to recover the lands lost in 1204, but his allies were crushed at Bouvines on 27 July 1214. The defeat ended his hopes of regaining Normandy and led to the baronial revolt and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-carta">Magna Carta</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-french-war-1213-1214.jpg" alt="Anglo-French War (1213–1214)" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Horace Vernet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_de_Bouvines_gagnee_par_Philippe_Auguste.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
